  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure builds in from the west through \nmost of this week behind the cold front continuing to push\noffshore. Temps will gradually warm through the week as heights\nbuild. By mid to late week highs will again be back into the \n80s for most of the area. A backdoor front will eventually cross\nthe FA THU, but at this time just looks to be a wind shift with\nthe column ahead of, along, and near the front being almost\ncompletely devoid of moisture.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A stronger cold front will push through the area\nFriday night, with strong high pressure building in for the weekend.\nFront looks moisture starved, but could bring sct shower \nchances. Cooler and drier airmass will build into the region \nthis weekend, feeling like fall, with highs mainly in the 60s\nand lows in the 40s/50s. N-NW winds continue to trend a bit \nstronger behind the front, which could bring dangerous marine \nconditions along with the potential for coastal impacts for\nvulnerable locations along OBX. Though too soon for any \nspecifics.",
